<!-- @agents-index Canonical project vocabulary: one row per domain noun in the four-column model. -->
# Taxonomy

The canonical vocabulary of the project. One row per term, one physical line per row. Bold appears only in the Term column.

## Product

| Term | Means | Not | Lives in |
|---|---|---|---|
| **proxy token** | A random value with the prefix `lpt_` that lets a client use the proxy; the binary stores only its SHA-256 hash, with a unique name and key=value tags. | A provider credential that the agent sends to the upstream; a GitHub token label. | `docs/specification/proxy.tokens.md`, `src/token/`, `src/cli/token.rs` |
| **bootstrap token** | The proxy token with the name `bootstrap` that `loupe serve` makes, replaces, or revokes at start from `LOUPE_BOOTSTRAP_TOKEN`. | A token from `loupe token create`, which cannot use the name bootstrap; the variable itself, which holds the raw value. | `docs/specification/proxy.tokens.md`, `src/token/bootstrap.rs` |
| **token gate** | The check between the route parser and the forwarder that accepts a request, or refuses it with 401, by the state of the table `proxy_tokens`: no-token mode while the table never held a row, required after the first row, closed when every row is revoked. | The allowlist, which refuses an unknown upstream with 404; redaction of provider credentials. | `docs/specification/proxy.tokens.md`, `src/token/gate.rs` |
| **provider account** | The identity of the account at the model provider, stored only as an HMAC-SHA256 under `LOUPE_ACCOUNT_KEY` of the first present source: an account ID header, the account UUID in `metadata.user_id`, or the credential; one row of `accounts`. | A proxy token, which identifies the client of the proxy, not the provider account. | `docs/specification/accounts.md`, `src/account/` |
| **exchange** | One request and its response that the proxy forwards and stores, with encrypted bodies and redacted credentials. | A call, which the parser finds inside an exchange. | `docs/specification/proxy.md`, `src/capture/` |
| **call** | One model call that the parser finds from the usage block in the response of an exchange, with its five token counts, model, and service tier; one row of `calls`. | An exchange, which is the raw stored request and response. | `docs/specification/parser.md`, `src/parse/` |
| **session** | The calls of one scope (agent label, proxy token ID, session key), stored as one or more segments; a subagent is its own session. | A segment, which is one run of the session with no gap above `LOUPE_IDLE_SECS`; a day record. | `docs/specification/parser.md`, `src/session/` |
| **segment** | One row of `sessions`: a run of calls in one session scope with no gap above `LOUPE_IDLE_SECS`; it closes on a gap or on idle, and a resumed conversation after a close starts the next segment. | A session, which can hold more than one segment; the day rule, which counts a session on each day that has a call and reads the start time of each call. | `docs/specification/parser.md`, `src/session/segment.rs` |
| **session key** | The first present source of session hint, session ID in `metadata.user_id`, `prompt_cache_key`, or opening hash, stored as an HMAC-SHA256 under `LOUPE_ACCOUNT_KEY` with its source name. | A session hint, which is only the first source; a session, which is the group of calls. | `docs/specification/parser.md`, `src/session/key.rs` |
| **session hint** | The HMAC-SHA256 of the first present session header that the capture stores on the exchange, with the header name. | A session key, which the parser selects and which can come from the body. | `docs/specification/parser.md`, `src/capture/session_hint.rs` |
| **day record** | The published totals of one day in `LOUPE_TZ`: tokens, calls, sessions, cost, unpriced calls, pull requests, lines, and a summary. | A session; a day with no calls and no GitHub activity, which has no record. | `docs/specification/days-public-api.md` |
| **upstream** | A named provider base URL in `upstreams.toml` that the proxy can forward to; the file is also the allowlist of hosts. | An agent label, which names the client, not the destination. | `docs/specification/proxy.md`, `src/proxy/upstreams.rs`, `upstreams.toml` |
| **agent label** | The name of the agent in the proxy route, for example `claude-code` or `pi`, from `/<agent>/<upstream>/<path>`. | An upstream, which names the provider. | `docs/specification/proxy.md`, `src/proxy/route.rs` |
| **capture limit** | The maximum count of bytes of one body that the capture keeps, set by `LOUPE_CAPTURE_MAX_BYTES` with the default 33554432; a larger body is forwarded in full and the stored copy is truncated with a flag. | The size of the forwarded body, which the proxy never limits; the capture queue size `LOUPE_CAPTURE_QUEUE`, which counts records, not bytes. | `docs/specification/proxy.md`, `src/capture/tap.rs` |
| **API-equivalent cost** | The cost of a call at the list price of the provider API from the vendored LiteLLM price file, also when the agent uses a subscription. | The price that the user paid for a subscription, which is the subscription cost. | `src/price/`, `docs/specification/cost.md` |
| **price commit** | The 40-hex commit of the vendored LiteLLM price file, embedded at build time and stored on each priced or unpriced call. | The commit of this repository. | `build.rs`, `src/price/`, `vendor/litellm/SOURCE.md`, `docs/specification/cost.md` |
| **subscription cost** | The real monthly price of a subscription from LOUPE_SUBSCRIPTION_<NAME>, pro-rated to one calendar day by the days of that month. | The API-equivalent cost of the calls. | `src/subscription/`, `docs/specification/cost.md` |
| **unpriced call** | A call with no matching price entry or a missing price field for a non-zero token count; its cost is null and it counts in `unpriced_calls`. | A call with a cost of zero. | `src/price/`, `docs/specification/cost.md` |
| **GitHub token label** | The `<LABEL>` part of a `LOUPE_GITHUB_TOKEN_<LABEL>` variable, recorded with each pull request so an analysis can group by it. | A proxy token; the GitHub token value, which stays in the environment. | `docs/specification/github.md` |
| **public API** | The open-CORS routes `GET /v1/days`, `GET /v1/days/{day}`, and `GET /healthz` that other sites can read. | The dashboard, which is a page that reads the public API. | `docs/specification/days-public-api.md` |
| **dashboard** | The page that the same binary serves at `GET /`, which reads `/v1/days` and shows the data. | The public API, which returns data and no page. | `docs/specification/dashboard.md` |

## Foundation

| Term | Means | Not | Lives in |
|---|---|---|---|
| **configuration source** | Where the loader got an effective value: one of `flag`, `env`, `file`, or `default`, in that order of precedence. | The file for the environment `config/<env>.toml`, which is one source only. | `docs/specification/configuration.md` |
| **pipeline entry point** | A script under `.agents/scripts/` that does one stage of the pipeline, for example `pipeline.test.sh`. | A platform thin caller, which only calls an entry point. | `.agents/scripts/`, `docs/specification/operations.md` |
| **verdict** | The result of `pipeline.verdict.sh`: one `status: passed` or `status: failed` line per stage, the times, and an exit code. | The result of one stage entry point alone. | `.agents/scripts/pipeline.verdict.sh`, `docs/specification/operations.md` |
